{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"e27c happy-oracle correction during handoff: the fsck routing test reached the real legacy auto-init seam after canonical parser work, but its fixture had not injected a tracker override. The acceptance contract requires canonical and legacy fsck to retain the same auto-init policy, so the test—not production—was corrected to bypass unrelated first-time provisioning. The original pre-implementation run was already RED earlier at the absent nested parser, and the fixture change cannot bypass that missing-parser condition. Worker was paused during the correction and explicitly instructed to preserve legacy auto-init."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786331778109498001,"uuid":"88ca690b-f271-4dda-a6f8-cc648d83c39e"}